RESULT: CONFIRMED FIXED. All three sub-claims hold, on-device, this cycle.

── (1) Exactly one node per row ─────────────────────────────────────────────
Live `uiautomator dump` pulled fresh this run
(NEARS-3701-settings-a11y-dump-cycle3.xml). Both rows are now a single
self-closing node with NO children at all (cycle-2's nested
`android.view.View` Focus-node leak is gone):

  <node index="4" class="android.widget.Switch" content-desc="Order updates,
        switch" checkable="true" checked="true" clickable="true"
        bounds="[96,1001][1248,1193]" />

  <node index="5" class="android.widget.Switch" content-desc="Offers and
        promotions, switch" checkable="true" checked="true" clickable="true"
        bounds="[96,1194][1248,1386]" />

Confirmed by direct regex scan of the raw dump for ANY node whose bounds
fall in/overlap the y-range [990,1400] (the two rows' combined span): exactly
2 matches total, one per row, neither with a second overlapping node. Total
node count in the file (24) matches `ui_nodes`' own parse count, so nothing
was silently dropped by a lossy driver layer.

Positive control (proves the dump instrument was live, not vacuously empty):
the "About Us" row (no semanticLabel set, setting_page.dart), bounds
