── Environment note ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
This worktree's suffixed install has no `google-services.json` (normal QA
state) — per the documented gotcha
(userapp-navigation-guide.md "pick_map_screen FAB / Firebase silent-fail"
section), a suffixed install with no Firebase config throws synchronously
inside `LocationController._saveDataAndFirebaseConfig` on the very FIRST
address-confirm action of a truly fresh cold start, silently blocking any
route past the location gate. Rather than force a fresh guest cold-start
through that known dead end, this run used the documented "unsuffixed
control boot" recipe (primary tree's `google-services.json` copied in
temporarily, `NEARS_PKG_SUFFIX` unset, `qa-run.sh` bypassed) on the same
already-acquired device lock, landing on an EXISTING logged-in session
(Sophie Davis) with a saved address already past the location gate — the
Settings screen and its two rows are identical DLS/app code regardless of
which boot path reached them; nothing about NEARS-3701's fix is
suffix/Firebase-dependent. Copied `google-services.json` removed after the
run per the gotcha's own cleanup instruction; suffixed package
`com.izzes.nears.nears_nears_3639_settings_dls_notificati` uninstalled at
teardown; unsuffixed `com.izzes.nears`'s process force-stopped but the
shared APK itself left installed (never uninstalled the base package).

NET: NEARS-3701 AC ("exactly one a11y node per row") IS NOW MET, on-device,
